-- =============================================================================
-- FILE: 002_seed_data.sql
-- PURPOSE: Import all existing records from SQLite into Supabase PostgreSQL.
--
-- HOW TO USE:
--   1. Make sure 001_create_schema.sql has already been run successfully.
--   2. Open Supabase → SQL Editor → New Query.
--   3. Paste the entire contents of this file and click RUN.
--
-- IMPORTANT:
--   Run this file ONLY ONCE on a fresh (empty) set of tables.
--   Running it a second time will cause duplicate-key errors because
--   the original id values are explicitly inserted.
--
-- OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE:
--   PostgreSQL SERIAL columns manage their own auto-increment counter.
--   To insert rows with specific id values we use:
--     INSERT INTO table (id, ...) OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE VALUES (...).
--   After this file runs, 003_set_sequences.sql resets each counter so
--   future inserts do not collide with the imported ids.
-- =============================================================================

